# Files tracked on main that the public release does not carry. export-ignore
# keeps them out of `git archive` and out of a forge's tag tarball, so the
# public tree is produced as an archive export of the release commit and these
# never reach it. One line per entry of DefaultStripAtPublish in
# test/internal/labstrings/published.go, in that list's own pattern syntax,
# and for a directory entry (`<dir>/**`) a second line for `<dir>` itself:
# the `/**` form excludes the files, but git archive still writes the
# directory's own entry, which tells the public tree the directory exists;
# test/tools/releasability-gate/export_test.go fails when an entry there is not
# excluded here, and the releasability gate fails on a tracked file it lists
# that this file does not export-ignore.
#
# Not covered: the Go module zip (built from the public repository's tag, so
# it is clean only because that tag's tree is the export) and a history push
# (every commit carries these files). See docs/release/public-releasability.md.

# Agent instructions and tool state, at any depth.
**/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
**/AGENTS.md export-ignore
**/.claude/** export-ignore
**/.claude export-ignore
**/.serena/** export-ignore
**/.serena export-ignore

# Internal workflows. The public ones are ci.yml, nightly.yml and release.yml.
.github/workflows/automerge.yml export-ignore
.github/workflows/code-review.yml export-ignore
.github/workflows/qwen-review.yml export-ignore
.github/workflows/batch.yml export-ignore

# Tests that read only an internal workflow, stripped with the file they test.
test/ci/workflows/batch_test.go export-ignore

# The fleet pattern set and its tests: they name the values the gate bans.
test/internal/labstrings/fleet.go export-ignore
test/internal/labstrings/fleet_test.go export-ignore
